@page id="bk-canon" rh="BACK MATTER · THE CANON REGISTER · 1 OF 2" m="DECIDED; FINAL RULINGS"
# What's fixed
Everything on this page is canon until you overrule it. The Final Rulings outrank every source file, and your own decisions outrank the rest of this book.
tabrl:
| Item | Ruling | Where it lands |
| Solomon's age | DECIDED: sixteen. The timeline's thirteen is SUPERSEDED. | Part II cast table, Part VI men |
| Leah and Eden | DECIDED: Leah is younger than Eden. | Part II cast table |
| Thomas | Left voluntarily (FR 3) | Part VI Commonwife marriage |
| Miriam | Reassigned after Thomas left (FR 0). Celeste has no proof she's alive (FR 16). | Part V, Part VI |
| Leah's assessment | DECIDED: Leah sat for an assessment. | Part VI Designation |
| The Prelate | Renamed under FR 33 so Hannah's daughter keeps the name Naomi. POSSIBLE: working name Aurelia. Never Huldah. | Part VI Temple |
| Crest | Dorian's uncle (FR 35). His claim came through survivorship (FR 39). | Parts V, VI |
| The removed heir | Elias's elder child, Dorian's parent, removed in 2061 (FR 35–36) | Part V |
| Dorian | 59 in 2104 (Ruling) | Parts V, VI |
| Calla's surname | Merritt (Ruling) | Part VIII |
| Children's status | By household registration, not parentage (FR 32) | Part VI |
| The eleven | Married down the elite ladder. Nobody goes home unassigned (FR 19). | Parts VI, VIII |
| Declining an assignment | A man may decline the whole assignment. It has happened twice (FR 28). | Part VI |
| The Declaration | FR 20–25, as printed in Part VIII | Part VIII |

