@page id="bk-sources" rh="BACK MATTER · SOURCES AND EDITIONS · 1 OF 5" m="SOURCE MARGIN; ALL PARTS"
# Where all of this came from
Every page carries a narrow source margin on its outer edge, in compressed form, author and short title. The compressed forms point to the full citations on the next pages. Nothing in a margin is a citation by itself.
rec:
Research | Unlabeled prose in Parts I to IV is research: the text says it, or the manuscript evidence shows it, and you can check it in any study Bible with a critical apparatus.
CONTESTED | Responsible scholars or traditions disagree. The dispute is printed, with the strongest case on each side, and no verdict.
INTERPRETATION · INFERENCE | A reading offered as a reading, or a conclusion drawn from your files that they don't state.
POSSIBLE | A TKC construction, about Dominion, the Temple or the manuscript, and not a claim about scripture. Test it before use.
DECIDED | A call you've made. Fixed until you rule otherwise.
k: On the secondary literature
The works listed are standard reference points and not endorsements of any one position. Where two disagree, and several do sharply, the companion prints the disagreement. Several are technical commentaries that assume Hebrew or Greek. You don't need them to use this book. They're listed so every claim can be traced.
tab:
| Translation I'm working from | Edition or printing | Used for |
